ore year  maybe two more years although the second  year is going to be  the fifth year option which will be  north of 20 million but until they they  pay carson wentz a huge contract they  could afford to to dump a lot of money  into le'veon bell's pockets  so the eagles are one of the teams you  would have to at least put on the  fringes of being in play  they didn't have jay ajayi for much of  last year he tore an acl from time to  time it felt like the running game was  kind of lost in the shuffle and we know  how important the running game is to  that equals offense so that is a team  that that maybe possibly should be  considered the jets are a team that  that we've been talking about really  from the get-go and i've i've believed  from the moment it looked like le'veon  bell was setting this up to get the free  agency the jets would be the team that  would pay le'veon bell for reasons  related to football and for reasons  unrelated to football because they're  trying to compete with the patriots  trying to compete with the giants  they're trying to sell tickets they're  trying to sell psls still and they have  a few years left with sam darnold under  a relatively small contract in  comparison to what he eventually will  have when he gets his second deal so pay  le'veon bell a bunch of money over the  next few years helps sam donald grow  into the quarterback he he needs to be  for the jets to be as good as they can  be so that makes a ton of sense plenty  of other eagles players noticed what  le'veon bell had to say  chris long had a gif of a smiling dwight  schrute and malcolm jenkins  had a picture with the words come  quickly on it so the eagles would like  to have le'veon bell the jets i think  would like to have le'veon bell there  aren't a ton of teams  that really need a workhorse running  back  uh but there are enough and all it takes  is two last year at the end of the day  it was the jets and the vikings that  were pursuing kirk cousins that was it 