ing  that young guy as your workhorse you  don't want le'veon bell to replace him  because you're going to be spending a  ton of money on le'veon bell and any  team that likes to go with two or three  running backs that team's not going to  want le'veon bell you know it and  something that we'll do for pft we'll go  through the standings we'll go through  the 32 teams and identify any team that  potentially could want them and more  importantly the teams that definitely  wouldn't the cowboys aren't going to  want him the vikings aren't going to  want him any team with a young workhorse  running back is not going to want  le'veon bell but again all it takes is  two  and i have a feeling it'll be more than  two  it may be  four or five by the time it's all said  and done the raiders could jump into  this who knows but le'veon bell is going  to get the contract that he couldn't get  in pittsburgh and and there will be  people who say well this contract  doesn't make up for the 14.5 million  that you lost last year but if it's got  significant guaranteed money if it's  better than the deal  that the steelers offered le'veon bell  in 2017 and 2018. remember the steelers  won't guarantee money beyond the first  year of the contract they won't do it  other teams will this is what le'veon  bell has been waiting for and one of the  big reasons he's not going to be back in  pittsburgh because the steelers will not  structure contracts the way that most if  not all other teams well i think the  the bears may be the only other team  that is careful about guaranteeing money  beyond that first year other teams will  do it someone will do it for le'veon  bell and le'veon bell is going to make a  ton of money on or before officially on  march 13 but he'll know on or before  march 13 where that money's coming from  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports

